811
01:30:18,510 --> 01:30:24,228
我们要查询的日期，比如 12 月 15 日、16 日、17 日等等。
dates where we are checking this for, like December 15, 16, 17, and so on.

812
01:30:24,816 --> 01:30:32,996
然后我们会看到总库存和总预订量，这能让我们知道还有多少房间可用。
And then we will see the total inventory and also total reserve, which will give us an idea on how many rooms we have available.

813
01:30:33,518 --> 01:30:42,628
在查询可用性时，如果你使用 SQL 数据库，假设查询 12 月 23 日到 27 日，我们将选择日期
When checking the availability, if you're using the SQL database, let's say, for December 23 to 27, we will select the date,

814
01:30:42,816 --> 01:30:50,576
总库存和总预订量（就是这一列），以及总库存，也就是可用的数量。
total inventory, and total reserved, which is this column here, and then the total inventory, which is the available.

815
01:30:50,894 --> 01:31:01,092
我们将从房型库存表中查询酒店 ID 和房型 ID 匹配的记录，并将日期设置为我们想要的范围。
We will select it from the room type inventory where the hotel ID and room type ID match, and we will set the date to be between the range that we want to.

816
01:31:01,582 --> 01:31:05,060
这将给出总预订量和总库存。
This will give us the total reserved and total inventory.

817
01:31:05,536 --> 01:31:14,336
通过这个，我们可以检查如果“总预订 + 待预订房间”仍然小于或等于总库存的话，
And by using this, we can check that if the total reserve plus rooms to book is still less than equal to the total inventory,

818
01:31:14,496 --> 01:31:15,812
我们就允许预订。
then we allow the booking.

819
01:31:16,176 --> 01:31:25,444
也就是说，如果这里是 100，这里是 92，那我们还有 8 个房间可用，如果用户只想预订一个房间的话，
Which means if let's say here we have 100 and here we have 92, so we still have eight rooms available, and if user is trying to book just one room,

820
01:31:25,776 --> 01:31:34,980
那就是 92 加 1，我们拿它和 100 进行对比，条件成立，我们就允许预订。
that will be 92 plus 1, and we are checking this against 100, so the condition will be true and we will allow the booking.

821
01:31:35,552 --> 01:31:43,552
回到最初的需求，既然我们允许比如 10% 的超量预订或者类似的比例，
And coming back to the initial requirements, since we allow let's say 10% overbooking or whatever that number is,

822
01:31:43,872 --> 01:31:46,832
我们可以把这个超量预订因子包含进来。
we can include that overbooking factor here.

823
01:31:46,992 --> 01:31:54,112
假设如果你允许 10% 的超量预订，那我们就允许 10%，就像这里说的这 10%。
Let's say, if you allow 10% overbooking, then we will allow 10 %, like said the 10% here.

824
01:31:54,414 --> 01:32:02,592
这意味着如果我们有 100 的总库存，我们就允许他们预订多达 110 间房。
meaning if we have 100 total inventory available, then we will allow them to book up to 110 rooms

825
01:32:02,752 --> 01:32:08,708
因为我们知道剩下的那 10 间在预订日期之前很可能会被取消。
because we know that the other 10 will probably be cancelled until the date of the reservation.

826
01:32:09,166 --> 01:32:12,900
最后，我们来讨论一下为什么选择关系型数据库。
And lastly, let's also discuss why we move with relational database.

827
01:32:13,072 --> 01:32:18,980
在这种情况下，我们已经稍微提到了这一点，但让我们深入探讨一下选择它的原因。
In this case, we kind of touched on this, but let's get a bit deeper in why we choose this.

828
01:32:19,630 --> 01:32:27,620
首先，我们这里最需要的是 ACID 保障，特别是 SQL 数据库的一致性。
So, first, the most important thing we need here is the ACID guarantees and specifically the consistency of SQL databases.

829
01:32:27,872 --> 01:32:33,392
这对我们防止重复预订问题非常重要，我们稍后会处理这个问题。
This is important for us for preventing double poking issues, which we will handle soon.

830
01:32:33,902 --> 01:32:37,988
从计算结果可以看出，这是一个非常读密集型的系统。
From the calculations, we can also see that this is a very read-heavy system.

831
01:32:38,478 --> 01:32:46,116
因此关系型数据库能很好地处理这类读取，而且我们始终可以用 Elasticsearch 来进行扩展。
So relational databases handle this kind of reads well, and we can always combine it with Elasticsearch for scaling it.

832
01:32:46,672 --> 01:32:56,452
但考虑到每秒查询数是 1000 次读，而只有 17 次写，这清楚地表明我们需要在这里使用 SQL 数据库
But with 1000 reads, queries per second versus 17 writes per second, this clearly shows that we need to go with an SQL database here

833
01:32:56,672 --> 01:33:01,220
并结合我们从 ACID 中需要的的一致性因素。
in combination with the consistency factor that we need from the ACID.

834
01:33:01,742 --> 01:33:09,712
而且这种方式下关系更清晰，比如房间、酒店、房型、预订、
And then the relationships are more clear this way, like between rooms, hotels, the room types, reservations,

835
01:33:09,952 --> 01:33:11,268
事务等等。
transactions, and so on.

836
01:33:11,792 --> 01:33:19,792
我们需要执行复杂的查询来检查房间的可用性，或者为了获取库存信息进行多次连接
And we'll need to make complex queries to check the availability of the rooms or make multiple joins for inventory

837
01:33:19,982 --> 01:33:23,812
与定价结合、按日期过滤、汇总总量等。
with pricing, filter by dates, aggregate totals, and so on.

838
01:33:24,142 --> 01:33:26,672
所以 SQL 也能很好地处理这些。
So SQL will handle this well as well.

839
01:33:26,832 --> 01:33:29,232
我们还需要处理并发问题。
We also need to handle the concurrency.

840
01:33:29,472 --> 01:33:35,872
我们已经讨论过第一个场景，即同一个用户尝试两次预订同一个房间。
We already discussed the first scenario where the same user is trying to book the same room twice.

841
01:33:36,174 --> 01:33:38,916
这里的解决方案就是使用那个预订键。
And the solution here is just to have that reservation key.

842
01:33:39,278 --> 01:33:45,060
这样任何第二次请求都会收到重复键错误，然后我们会返回现有的预订。
So any second request will get duplicate key error and we will return the existing reservation.

843
01:33:45,232 --> 01:33:48,192
所以这是一个我们可以解决的简单问题。
So that's the simple one that we can solve.

844
01:33:48,462 --> 01:33:57,860
但第二个场景是：有两个不同的用户试图预订同一种房型，而该酒店只剩下一个位置了。
But then the second scenario is we have two different users who are trying to book the same room type, which is only one spot left for that hotel.

845
01:33:58,318 --> 01:34:07,632
如果你了解 SQL 的隔离级别，默认情况下它是“读已提交”，而在“读已提交”隔离级别下仍然会发生并发 Bug。
And if you know about the SQL isolation layers, by default this will be read committed, and concurrency bugs still happen at read-committed

846
01:34:07,792 --> 01:34:13,604
这意味着你只有在其他事务提交后才能看到数据。
isolation layer, which means that you only see data after other transactions commit.

847
01:34:13,952 --> 01:34:20,432
但在你读取（比如检查可用性）和写入（即预订房间）之间存在一个间隙。
But there is a gap between when you read, like check the availability, and when you write, which is you book the room.

848
01:34:20,672 --> 01:34:29,152
在这个间隙中，可能会有两个不同的事务在运行，比如用户 A 读取总预订数，他看到还有一个房间可用
And in that gap you might have two different transaction happening, like user A reads the total reserved, he sees that one room is available

849
01:34:29,312 --> 01:34:30,756
因为总数是 100。
because the total is 100.

850
01:34:31,246 --> 01:34:39,152
而用户 B 也读取并看到有 99 间房已预订，还有 100 个可用，这意味着还有一个可用。
And user B also reads and sees that there are 99 rooms reserved and 100 available, which means that there is one available.

851
01:34:39,312 --> 01:34:48,420
所以对于他们两个来说，检查都显示成功，也就是说条件成立，这意味着我们允许他们继续进行预订。
So for both of them, the checks shows successful, like the condition is true, which means that we allow them to proceed with the booking.

852
01:34:49,006 --> 01:34:58,660
因此，“读已提交”本身对于预订是不安全的，因为两个事务都可能读取到有效数据，通过检查，然后互相覆盖。
So read committed by itself is unsafe for bookings because two transactions can both read valid data, pass checks, and then overwrite each other.

853
01:34:59,054 --> 01:35:01,508
这就是“重复预订”发生的原因。
And that's exactly how double bookings happen.

854
01:35:01,742 --> 01:35:05,316
针对这个问题，在这种情况下我们有两种主要的处理方法。
As a solution to this, we have two main approaches in this case.

855
01:35:05,838 --> 01:35:16,672
其中一种方法是我们可以使用“可串行化”隔离级别，这意味着在代码层面开始事务时，我们可以将隔离级别设置为“可串行化”。
One approach here is that we can use serializable isolation layer, which means that when beginning the transaction at the code level, we can set the isolation layer to be serializable.

856
01:35:16,832 --> 01:35:18,724
默认情况下它是“读已提交”。
By default, it is read committed.

857
01:35:19,278 --> 01:35:30,496
这种方法实现简单，而且对于低 TPS（即每秒事务数）来说效果很好，因为如果你没有那么高的并发量，这些事务就不会互相阻塞。
This is simple to implement and it will work fine for low TPS, meaning transactions per second, because these won't be blocking each other if you don't have that much high volume.

858
01:35:30,766 --> 01:35:33,572
所以在那种情况下使用“可串行化”是可以的。
So it's fine to use serializable in that case.

859
01:35:34,190 --> 01:35:37,924
它的缺点是事务会互相阻塞。
The downsides to this is that transactions will block each other.

860
01:35:38,256 --> 01:35:41,936
所以如果你有高 TPS，那么这种方式就无法很好地扩展。
So if you have high TPS, then this won't scale well.

861
01:35:42,158 --> 01:35:48,196
而且如果你以不同的顺序锁定多个资源，还会引入潜在的死锁。
And also you introduce potential deadlocks if locking multiple resources in different orders.

862
01:35:48,750 --> 01:35:58,628
不过，你可以使用，比如说，锁超时，并将其设置为某个数值，以防止无限期等待，同时保持事务简短。
However, you can use, let's say, lock timeouts and set it to some number to prevent indefinite weights and also keep the transactions short.

863
01:35:59,216 --> 01:36:09,220
但即便如此，在这种情况下还有一个更好的解决方案，就是使用“读已提交”隔离级别（仍是默认模式），并结合行锁。
But still, there is a better solution in this case, which is to use read committed isolation layer, which is still the default mode, in combination with row locking.

864
01:36:09,582 --> 01:36:21,136
这就是当你使用“选择并更新”时的情况，它用于在检查和预订过程中锁定库存行。这样其他用户就必须等待他们的轮到。
This is when you're using select for update and it is used to lock the inventory rows while we are checking and booking them. So that other users have to wait their turn.

865
01:36:21,216 --> 01:36:29,412
如果有两个事务试图写入同一行，第二个事务需要等待这个事务处理完成。
If you have two transactions who try to log the same row, the second one needs to wait for this transaction to be processed.

866
01:36:29,806 --> 01:36:41,924
但如果还有其他不尝试写入这一行的事务，它们就可以继续前进，基本上它们可以并行运行，而不是像“可串行化”那样
But if there are other transactions which are not trying to write to this same row, then they are free to move forward and basically they can go in parallel instead of the serializable

867
01:36:42,096 --> 01:36:44,484
要求事务一个接一个地执行。
where the transactions need to go one by one.

868
01:36:45,070 --> 01:36:52,096
因此，这里的“for update”通过将访问特定行序列化来防止竞态条件。
So the for update here prevents the race condition by serializing access to specific rows in this

869
01:36:52,096 --> 01:36:58,340
“读已提交”仍然是 PostgreSQL 的默认值，在这里运行良好。
case. The read committed is still the PostgreSQL's default and works fine here.

870
01:36:58,766 --> 01:37:08,388
如果你有低 TPS，且每秒有多少流量写入数据库并不多，那么使用“可串行化”也是可以的。
And serializable is fine to be used if you have low TPS and not that much traffic coming to write to the database every second.

871
01:37:09,134 --> 01:37:18,628
下一阶段是讨论系统的扩展，比如数据库分片、是否需要分片、缓存策略，以及我们如何优化 Elasticsearch 查询。
The next phase is talking about scaling the system, things like database sharding, whether it's needed, caching strategy, how we are going to optimize the Elasticsearch queries.

872
01:37:18,990 --> 01:37:20,836
那么我们从数据库分片开始。
So let's start from the database sharding.

873
01:37:21,326 --> 01:37:31,364
由于我们需要处理每秒 1000 次查询和 17 次事务，最终我们需要对这些数据进行分片，这在执行典型查询所需时间变长时会变得显而易见。
Since we're going to handle 1000 queries per second and 17 transactions per second, we need to eventually shard this, and that will be obvious

874
01:37:31,696 --> 01:37:35,492
到那时就会很明显。
by the time it takes for typical queries to run.

875
01:37:36,016 --> 01:37:38,436
这里有一些可以拆分的表。
And there are tables here that we can split.

876
01:37:39,022 --> 01:37:47,172
涉及到分片时，关键的决策是选择什么作为分片键，以及根据哪个字段进行分片。
When it comes to sharding, the important decision is what will be the shard key and by which field you are going to shard.

877
01:37:47,726 --> 01:37:50,852
其中一个例子是按酒店 ID 进行分片。
One example here is to shard it by hotel ID.

878
01:37:51,342 --> 01:37:59,716
为什么？因为大多数查询都会先按酒店过滤以查看其位置，判断是否符合搜索条件的过滤条件，
Why? Because most queries will filter by hotel first to see their location, whether it matches with the search query filter,

879
01:38:00,096 --> 01:38:05,092
然后他们才会获取该酒店可用的房型。
and then they are going to fetch the room types available in this hotel.

880
01:38:05,582 --> 01:38:13,056
一个酒店的所有数据仍将保留在同一个分片中，因此我们不会出现跨分片的连接。
All data for one hotel will still stay on the same shard, so we will not be cross-sharding the joints.

881
01:38:13,296 --> 01:38:17,124
这也能支持分片内的本地事务。
And this will also enable local transactions within the shard.

882
01:38:17,710 --> 01:38:23,376
对于初始部署，我们可以使用取模分片，这是分片的一种公式。
For initial deployment, we can use modulo sharding, which is the formula for sharding.

883
01:38:23,456 --> 01:38:32,196
所以分片编号将等于这个结果，最初不是一致性哈希，而仅仅是酒店 ID 的哈希值
So the shard number will be equal to this, won't be consistent hash initially, so it will be just the hash of the hotel ID

884
01:38:32,496 --> 01:38:35,876
结合我们拥有的分片数量。
in combination with the number of shards that we will have.

885
01:38:36,366 --> 01:38:40,452
当你确定分片数量不会经常变动时，这种方式效果很好。
This will work well when you know your shard count won't change often.

886
01:38:40,814 --> 01:38:48,896
所以如果我们决定将这每秒 1000 次的读取查询分布到 16 个分片中，那么每个分片大约会有
So if we decide to, let's say, split this 1000 read queries per second between 16 shards, then this will range about

887
01:38:49,262 --> 01:38:56,132
62 次读请求（即每秒查询数）和 1 次写事务。
62 reads meaning queries per second and one writes transactions per second per shard.

888
01:38:56,336 --> 01:38:59,684
在这种情况下，取模分片可以很好地工作。
So in that case, the modulo sharding will work fine.

889
01:39:00,016 --> 01:39:07,012
之后，如果需要减少数据迁移，我们可以在那时引入一致性哈希。
And then later, that is where we can integrate consistent sharding if needed to minimize the data movement.

890
01:39:07,246 --> 01:39:16,496
取模分片的问题在于，如果我们决定增加另一个数据库，比如编号为 17 的，这将要求我们重新洗牌
So the thing with modulo sharding is that if we decide to add another database, let's say number 17, this will require us to reshuffle

891
01:39:16,656 --> 01:39:19,428
从 1 到 16 的几乎所有数据。
almost all the data from 1 to 16.

892
01:39:19,854 --> 01:39:27,936
而如果使用一致性哈希，只有大约 1/17 的数据会移动。
Whereas if we use consistent hashing, this only moves about one of the 17th of the data.

893
01:39:28,654 --> 01:39:33,444
也就是那些即将存储在第 17 个分片中的数据。
Which is the data that is going to be stored in the 17th shard.

894
01:39:33,966 --> 01:39:39,428
你可以查看系统设计课程中的相关视频，在那里我讲解了一致性哈希。
And you can check out the video in the system design course where I talk about consistent hashing.

895
01:39:39,918 --> 01:39:50,752
基本上，它使用一个哈希环，其中服务器和键都映射到圆上的点，每个键都会进入环上顺时针方向的下一个服务器。
Basically, it uses a hash ring where both servers and keys map to points on a circle, and each key goes to the next server clockwise to the ring.

896
01:39:50,894 --> 01:39:59,712
如果你有一个这样的环，计算出的键落在这里，那么离它最近的服务器就在这里，
So if you have a ring like this, then you calculated the key which is ending up here, and the closest server to that is here,

897
01:39:59,872 --> 01:40:02,180
那么这个数据就会存储在那台服务器上。
then this will be stored in that server.

898
01:40:02,734 --> 01:40:10,948
因此，使用一致性哈希时，增加新服务器只会影响它与前一个服务器（即编号为 16 的）之间的键。
So with consistent hashing, adding a new server only affects the keys between it and the previous server, which is the number 16.

899
01:40:11,278 --> 01:40:16,032
而使用取模分片时，你基本上需要重新洗牌所有数据。
Whereas with modulo sharding, you need to basically reshuffle all the data.

900
01:40:16,238 --> 01:40:28,036
所以当分片数量较少时，取模分片是可行的选择。如果你知道通常会向数据库添加新分片，那么一致性哈希是更好的解决方案。
So with small number of shards, modulo sharding is the way to go. And if you know that you will be typically adding new shards to the database, then consistent hashing is a better solution here.

901
01:40:28,430 --> 01:40:32,612
现在来看看我们可以为酒店使用的缓存策略。
Now let's see the caching strategy that we can use for the hotels.

902
01:40:33,262 --> 01:40:40,388
我们需要在 Redis 或 Memcache 中缓存热门库存数据，以便进行智能失效处理。
We will need to cache the hot inventory data in Redis or Memcache for smart invalidation.

903
01:40:40,878 --> 01:40:50,592
